---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import StarCTA from '../../components/StarCTA.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="SCS Agent Skills"
	description="Four Agent Skills that let an AI assistant build, review, version, and compile your SCS context, with you confirming every change."
>
	<Nav />
	<div class="plugin-page">
		<div class="plugin-hero">
			<p class="hero-eyebrow">New in SCS 0.7.0</p>
			<h1>SCS Agent Skills</h1>
			<p>
				Four skills let an AI assistant build and maintain your guidance for AI. It runs the
				interview, drafts the rules, reviews them, and versions and compiles them. You confirm
				every change, and a person you name releases every version.
			</p>
			<div class="hero-ctas">
				<a href="/docs/getting-started/quick-start" class="btn btn-primary">Install the Skills</a>
				<a href="/docs/skills/overview" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the docs</a>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
			<h2>One workflow, with a person in charge</h2>
			<p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 60ch;">
				Interview &rarr; Draft &rarr; Consolidate &rarr; Section owners and review package &rarr; Review &rarr; Release &rarr; Compile.
				The skills carry the conversation and the judgment. The SCS tools do every write, and
				each change is shown as a dry run before it's made.
			</p>
			<div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>scs-domain</h3>
					<p>Sets up and maintains the rules for all of your organization's work, or your own, from interview to a compiled version.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>scs-project</h3>
					<p>Adds the rules for one piece of work, reviews them against the Domain, and never loosens the Domain's rules.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>scs-validate</h3>
					<p>Runs the automated checks at any time, explains the results in plain language, and proposes fixes.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>scs-explain</h3>
					<p>Explains where the work stands, a rule and where it came from, a compiled artifact, or a message. Writes a review package for the people who review a bundle.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="section-divider" />

		<section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
			<h2>Get started</h2>
			<div class="install-block">
				<p>Install the tools</p>
				<code>pip install "scs-tools==0.7.0"</code>
			</div>
			<p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; max-width: 60ch;">
				Then copy the four skills from the spec repository's <code>skills/</code> directory into
				Claude Code, or upload them to Claude (claude.ai). Python 3.11 or later and git are
				required. The skills use an open format, but so far they have been tried only in
				Claude Code and Claude.
			</p>
		</section>

		<hr class="section-divider" />

		<section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
			<h2>What you can count on</h2>
			<div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>You release</h3>
					<p>The skills never choose who releases a version, never take one from git configuration, and never record the AI. Formal approval stays in your own system, citing the version and its digest.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>You own it</h3>
					<p>Your context is plain files in your own git repository, not locked into a vendor.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>You can check it</h3>
					<p>Every rule records where it came from, and every version carries a digest, so a later edit is detected.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Your reviewers can read it</h3>
					<p>Each section names its owner. A review package shows every rule word for word, with the exact line the AI receives, in one HTML file.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="section-divider" />

		<section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
			<h2>Coming from scs-vibe or scs-team?</h2>
			<p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 60ch;">
				The plugins were removed in 0.7.0. They wrote context into application repositories,
				while 0.7 keeps it in its own Domain repository with approved versions. Start a Domain with
				<code>scs-domain</code> and give it your existing <code>CLAUDE.md</code> and rules files as
				source documents.
			</p>
		</section>

		<hr class="section-divider" />

		<section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
			<StarCTA />
		</section>
	</div>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
